## Commands
- Install: `pnpm i`
- Dev: `pnpm dev`
- Test one file: `pnpm vitest run path/to/file.test.ts`
- Typecheck + lint (run before every commit): `pnpm check`

## Engineering standard
- Write the smallest change that fully solves the task. Reuse before writing; no speculative abstractions.
- Never cut: input validation, authorization, error handling at boundaries, timeouts, tests.
- Plan first (docs/plans/<feature>.md) for anything touching more than 2 files; wait for approval.
- Bug fix = failing test first. Never report "done" without running `pnpm check` and tests.
- Security rules: see .claude/rules/security.md. Production rules: .claude/rules/code-quality.md.

## Conventions
- TypeScript strict; no `any`. Zod for all external input.
- Handlers in `src/routes/`, business logic in `src/services/`, queries in `src/db/`.
- IMPORTANT: never edit `src/generated/`; run `pnpm codegen`.
- Conventional commits; one logical change per commit.

